        { "host": "B", "text": "The paper reports it outperforms state-of-the-art foundation models across 26 of 30 diagnostic tasks. In multicentre retrospective and prospective validation across six independent cohorts of women, it achieves up to 99% sensitivity for clinically relevant lesion detection, with what the authors call acceptable specificity across sites." },
